Subject: [cuentapepas] YOLOX COCOEvaluator: use the reference pycocotools COCOeval

YOLOX 6ddff48 imports COCOeval_opt unconditionally and only falls back on ImportError, but
instantiating it JIT-builds a C++ op (torch.utils.cpp_extension: needs Ninja and a C++ compiler,
and writes to the user cache dir on C:). Without them the first evaluation raises RuntimeError
and training aborts. Always use pycocotools, the implementation `cuentapepas eval` reports.
Applied by tools/setup-yolox.sh.
---
diff --git a/yolox/evaluators/coco_evaluator.py b/yolox/evaluators/coco_evaluator.py
index e218c74..1cad277 100644
--- a/yolox/evaluators/coco_evaluator.py
+++ b/yolox/evaluators/coco_evaluator.py
@@ -290,12 +290,10 @@ class COCOEvaluator:
                 _, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp()
                 json.dump(data_dict, open(tmp, "w"))
                 cocoDt = cocoGt.loadRes(tmp)
-            try:
-                from yolox.layers import COCOeval_opt as COCOeval
-            except ImportError:
-                from pycocotools.cocoeval import COCOeval
-
-                logger.warning("Use standard COCOeval.")
+            # cuentapepas patch: `COCOeval_opt` always imports, but instantiating it JIT-builds a C++ op
+            # (needs Ninja + a C++ compiler, writes to the user cache dir) and raises RuntimeError without them.
+            # Use the reference pycocotools implementation, the same one `cuentapepas eval` reports.
+            from pycocotools.cocoeval import COCOeval
 
             cocoEval = COCOeval(cocoGt, cocoDt, annType[1])
             cocoEval.evaluate()
